  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "How long could you survive with no income starting tomorrow? Your emergency fund decides. Let's climb the levels.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "lock",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "clock"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "$0 to 2 years",
            "saved."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "At zero, one surprise bill becomes debt. At a few months, you can weather a layoff. At two years, you're nearly untouchable.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "rows",
          "kicker": "What each level survives",
          "rows": [
            {
              "rank": "1",
              "name": "$0",
              "value": "fragile",
              "note": "one bill = debt",
              "color": "#c0392b",
              "bar": 1.0
            },
            {
              "rank": "2",
              "name": "1 month",
              "value": "a scare",
              "note": "barely a buffer",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.7
            },
            {
              "rank": "3",
              "name": "6 months",
              "value": "a layoff",
              "note": "the standard goal",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.45
            },
            {
              "rank": "4",
              "name": "2 years",
              "value": "anything",
              "note": "near-untouchable",
              "color": "#1f7a3d",
              "bar": 0.25
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "An emergency fund is cash set aside purely for the unexpected.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-efund",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · emergency fund"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The reality is grim. Around forty percent of Americans can't cover a four hundred dollar surprise in cash.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "lock",
          "big": "40%",
          "label": "can't cover a $400 emergency",
          "props": [
            "x",
            "fire"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "And the average job search after a layoff runs about five months.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-unemployment",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · unemployment"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Which is exactly why the classic target is three to six months of expenses.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "lock",
          "big": "3–6 mo",
          "label": "the classic target",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "check"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Park it somewhere safe and liquid, like a money market account.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-mma",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · money market account"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The buffer isn't about being wealthy, it's about how many bad weeks you can absorb.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Weeks you can absorb",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "clock"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Building it starts with a budget that leaves something behind.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-budget",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · budget"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s9"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So honestly, with no income, how long could you actually last?",
